<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-MEN'S DOWNHILL TRAINING TIMES.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-MEN'S DOWNHILL TRAINING TIMES.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading times in the</p>
<p>first official training session for the men's downhill at the</p>
<p>Alpine skiing world championships on Tuesday (piste length 3,299</p>
<p>metres, vertical drop 914 metres):</p>
<p> 1. Fritz Strobl (Austria)   1 minute 53.88 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Luc Alphand (France)		1:53.99</p>
<p> 3. Werner Franz (Austria)	    1:54.33</p>
<p> 4. Hannes Trinkl (Austria)	   1:54.47</p>
<p> 5. Andreas Schifferer (Austria)    1:54.76</p>
<p> 6. Patrick Ortlieb (Austria)	 1:54.78</p>
<p> 7. Josef Strobl (Austria)	    1:54.82</p>
<p> 8. Pietro Vitalini (Italy)	   1:55.03</p>
<p> 9. Kristian Ghedina (Italy)	  1:55.51</p>
<p> 10.Luca Cattaneo (Italy)	     1:55.88</p>
<p> 11.Jean-Luc Cretier (France)	 1:55.91</p>
<p> 12.Guenther Mader (Austria)	  1:56.41</p>
<p> 13.Alessandro Fattori (Italy)	1:56.53</p>
<p> 14.Lasse Kjus (Norway)		 1:56.61</p>
<p> 15.Jason Rosener (U.S.)		1:56.64</p>
